LuaSQL SQLite3 driver: a query with no rows returns no row. Upstream candidate.

conn:execute() steps the statement once and creates a cursor also when that
step returns SQLITE_DONE. The first cursor:fetch() then returned a row of
NULLs: cursor:fetch({}, "a") returned a table, so code that tests the result
for nil saw a row. The first fetch now finalizes the cursor when the
statement has already run to completion.

--- a/src/ls_sqlite3.c	2026-10-09 22:16:36
+++ b/src/ls_sqlite3.c	2026-10-09 22:16:45
@@ -170,6 +170,9 @@
           return finalize(L, cur);
    } else {
       cur->first_fetch = 0;
+      /* conn:execute() already stepped once: SQLITE_DONE means no rows */
+      if (!sqlite3_stmt_busy(vm))
+          return finalize(L, cur);
    }
 
   if (lua_istable (L, 2))
